# Data Layer

## Architecture

`NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_MODE` → `getDataProvider()` → `MockDataProvider` | `AmplifyDataProvider`

Config: `src/lib/config/env.ts`, `src/lib/config/data-mode.ts`
Factory: `src/lib/data/factory.ts`
Hooks: `src/lib/data/hooks.ts` (`useDataProvider`, `useAsyncData`)

## Adding or changing an entity — touch all five

1. `src/lib/data/types.ts` — entity + `Create*` / `Update*` types
2. `src/lib/data/provider.ts` — interface methods
3. `src/lib/data/amplify/provider.ts` — `client.models.*` CRUD
4. `src/lib/data/amplify/mappers.ts` — Amplify record → domain type
5. `src/lib/data/mock/provider.ts` (+ `seed.ts` / `store.ts` if needed)

## Amplify provider

```ts
import type { Schema } from "../../../../amplify/data/resource";
const client = generateClient<Schema>();
```

Map `createdAt` / `updatedAt` in mappers; handle nullable FKs explicitly.

## Modes

| Mode | Command | Notes |
|------|---------|-------|
| mock | `pnpm dev:local` | In-memory; resets on restart |
| amplify | `pnpm dev:auth` | Requires `pnpm sandbox` first |
| localstack | — | **Not implemented**; falls back to mock |

Do not build features that require `localstack` without implementing a real provider.

## Existing entities

PoolProfile, WaterTest, ChemicalDose, Equipment, MaintenanceTask, PoolNote — all owner-scoped via `poolProfileId`.
